    "Scouting Notes": "Cantrelle was the Brewers 5th round selection in the 2020 COVID Draft. He was known for his contact skills and ability to play a little of everything in the infield. Thus far, the bat to ball skills have not really lived up to the expectations, as shown by his batting average of .192 and 25% K rate for the season. Despite that, Cantrelle is sitting at a 116 wRC+, thanks to an absurd walk rate of 23%, which gives him an OBP of .390 and he's shown some power, to the tune of 12 doubles and 7 HR. Cantrelle has also stolen 25 bases in 32 attempts. \n\nThe hit tool might be worse than expected, but the ability to draw walks, hit some XBH's , steal bases and play average to above average defense at 3 infield positions, gives Cantrelle a clear path to MLB. If the hit tool comes around to what it was expected to be, then it would not be shocking to see him as a long time utility player in the majors.",
